# The NIST StRD reference datasets are byte-exact copies of what NIST publishes, and their SHA-256 is
# recorded in backend/tests/reference_data/nist/manifest.json and re-hashed on every test run
# (backend/tests/nist/test_nist_manifest.py). git's autocrlf must never rewrite their line endings on
# checkout — on a Windows working tree that turns the committed LF into CRLF and every hash test fails,
# with no code change. Treating them as binary keeps the bytes on disk equal to the committed bytes on
# every platform, which is exactly the "stable across platforms and git autocrlf settings" guarantee
# fetch_nist.py's CRLF->LF normalisation is meant to give.
backend/tests/reference_data/nist/**/*.dat -text
